No Bitcoin Core C++ source is present in this module. The script interpreter
itself is clean-room from the published consensus rules and the BIPs; see this
module's README "Provenance" note. What is reproduced here, and only here, is
conformance DATA — which is precisely why the notice lives beside it.

The sibling `bitcointx` module cites Bitcoin Core as a design reference for the
legacy sighash algorithm; that is a design-reference record and lives in that
module's own `README.md` `Provenance:` statement, not here, because nothing of
theirs is reproduced there.

